  "shared_entries": [
    {
      "path": "RESEARCH.md",
      "entry_sha256": "4fbca9518b3dad8a87b6b70cfdb48ed05f4b69699ca3609c91de5447e99e4e46",
      "entry": "**Explicit generative foundation and situated consequences, 7 October 2026.** [The direct foundational continuation](_process/research/2026-10-05-generative-foundation-review/root-foundation/GENERAL-GENERATIVE-REQUIREMENT-INTEGRATION.md#direct-foundational-continuation-and-an-explicit-starting-point) integrates an affirmative argument, substantive counterreview and a primary biological correspondence after Ren's generation-axiom clarification. One proposed practical axiom makes both positive generative significance and its relevance to choices explicit; the existing checked general laws then support situational reasoning without a separate moral axiom per case. Earlier formation can remain operative during dormancy, so living dependence does not require constant production by every bearer. **Scope:** an explicit-premise formulation and application structure, with no new theorem or compiler run. Universal empirical coverage, independent first warrant and mixed practical comparisons remain unfinished; the full objective is preserved."
    },
    {
      "path": "theories/shengsheng-buxi-generative-existence/README.md",
      "entry_sha256": "cbacd891a4464e36eece8b4aa1e232241783d7dbe5d61f6f6b681bfc652b2f5a",
      "entry": "**Explicit foundation → situated consequences, 7 October 2026.** [The practical formulation](unified-2026-10-05/UNIFIED-ETHICAL-GROUNDING.md#from-an-explicit-foundation-to-situated-requirements) states generative significance and choice-specific relevance as an explicit proposed premise, then applies the existing general dependency results. [Argument, counterreview and living correspondence](../../_process/research/2026-10-05-generative-foundation-review/root-foundation/GENERAL-GENERATIVE-REQUIREMENT-INTEGRATION.md#direct-foundational-continuation-and-an-explicit-starting-point) retain alternative realizations, finite fulfillment, dormant capacities and differentiated response. This is a minimal explicit-premise framework; full physical coverage, independent universal warrant and mixed comparisons remain unfinished. No new mathematical proof is claimed."
    },
    {
      "path": "theories/shengsheng-buxi-generative-existence/unified-2026-10-05/GENERATIVE-GROUNDING.md",
      "entry_sha256": "c3e384545ee9613a1c22f86b1659a8624ca4c5810a0e45a0dcaf148935a58c43",
      "entry": "**Direct foundational continuation, 7 October 2026:** [The integrated assessment](../../../_process/research/2026-10-05-generative-foundation-review/root-foundation/GENERAL-GENERATIVE-REQUIREMENT-INTEGRATION.md#direct-foundational-continuation-and-an-explicit-starting-point) now connects Ren's explicit generation premise to a practical formulation and the checked general situational consequences. Its living investigation distinguishes earlier formation, continuing efficacy and required reconstruction; a bounded primary biological comparison supports that distinction. Universal address is visible in the proposed normative scope, not inferred from causal origin. Independent first warrant, full living-domain correspondence and mixed practical judgment remain open; these are the next substantive dependencies, with no new proof or unchanged compiler rerun."
    },
    {
      "path": "theories/shengsheng-buxi-generative-existence/unified-2026-10-05/UNIFIED-ETHICAL-GROUNDING.md",
      "entry_sha256": "db8f166b436f8cef3713f78d895b9216f2d9b3101481f4f2acc2fac244976b06",
      "entry": "## From an explicit foundation to situated requirements\n\n7 October 2026. [The direct continuation](../../../_process/research/2026-10-05-generative-foundation-review/root-foundation/GENERAL-GENERATIVE-REQUIREMENT-INTEGRATION.md#direct-foundational-continuation-and-an-explicit-starting-point) develops the explicit-premise route through an affirmative argument, substantive counterreview and a primary living-dependency assessment. Its proposed practical axiom states that a choice's actual contribution to living and the conditions of further living counts in its favor, while undermining those relations counts against it, retaining the connected history's differentiated effects and finite achievements. This is AI-authored practical elaboration of Ren's direction. Both favorable significance and relevance to choices are disclosed normative commitments; universal address is not deduced from causal origin.\n\nOne common foundation can therefore support situational reasoning without a new moral axiom for each response. Identify the actual future, explain its constituting relations, apply the checked necessity result where inherited provision is insufficient, and establish adequate realization on one history. A required continuation can require an adequate response without requiring one particular sufficient recipe or equal contribution from every participant. Mere favor does not establish duty; dependence alone does not allocate responsibility or authorize compulsion. Actual support, alternatives, losses and legitimate completion remain within the appraisal.\n\nThe living investigation distinguishes earlier formation from current exercise and recurrent reconstruction. Its bounded primary dormancy comparison supports the continued efficacy of earlier formed conditions, while leaving universal recurrence and full-domain correspondence unproved. Retention, rest and succession therefore cannot be excluded by requiring every bearer to produce continuously. A wider boundary can reveal omitted generativity, but does not itself prove that inherited conditions will be exhausted.\n\n**完成范围：明确前提下的共同实践框架，以及它与既有一般证明的接续；没有将公理本身证明为普遍必然。** A minimal directional axiom leaves some mixed comparisons unresolved; incomparability alone implies neither permission nor prohibition. The direct attempt to infer favorable authority from whole explanatory inclusion remains unsuccessful. The stronger universal objective is preserved, alongside positive development of the explicit-premise theory. No new theorem or compiler run is claimed.\n"
    }
  ],
